+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+[The 2026-08-08 non-goal ADR](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) confirmed NG-4 and NG-5 as deliberate product decisions. NG-5 covered two operations under one row: changing a booked visit and cancelling one. It also set the condition for revisiting either row — an explicit owner decision recorded at intake, never a request reopening the row by implication.
+
+That decision arrived on 2026-08-31. Visits could be created and never corrected, so a mistyped date or description stood permanently.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-5 whole.** Rejected by the owner: a record that cannot be corrected is a defect the sample teaches by accident.
+2. **Open NG-5 entirely,** allowing cancellation as well. Rejected: cancellation still adds lifecycle state the sample carries nowhere else, and the create and update flows already teach the pattern.
+3. **Split the row and narrow it to correction** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-5 now declines cancellation alone. Correcting a booked visit's date or description is in scope, recorded as `REQ-VIS-003`.
+
+A correction is judged by the same rules as a booking, and it changes the visit in place. The vocabulary follows: `docs/ubiquitous-language.md` separates a visit correction from a visit cancellation, so a later request names which one it means.
+
+The owner deferred the visible way in to the correction form. `REQ-VIS-003` adds no link on the owner's record; a follow-up request may add one. The deferral is a decision, not an omission.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The sample no longer demonstrates forward-only correction without exception. Visits join owners and pets as records that can be corrected; nothing is deleted or cancelled.
+- NG-4 is untouched, and the rest of the 2026-08-08 decision stands.
+- The form is reachable by its address alone until a follow-up request adds a way in. A reader browsing the pages will not find the capability.
+- Two questions open with the narrowing: whether a past-dated visit needs correcting, and whether the form gets a visible way in. Both are recorded in the PRD's Open Questions.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [PRD Visits](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the capability the narrowing admits.
